  "clarifying_question": null,
  "summary": "No listed instrument is fully configured out-of-the-box to measure crown-to-zirconia bond strength directly, though the universal mechanical testing system (EQ15) can potentially be used if appropriate custom grips or fixtures are acquired. Dedicated dental bond strength testing techniques and specialized jigs are typically required to reliably evaluate resin cement adhesion."
}

{
  "measurement_needs": [
    "fibroblast cell number",
    "surface area coverage over time in culture plates"
  ],
  "objective_met": true,
  "recommendations": [
    {
      "instrument_id": "EQ09",
      "role": "primary",
      "technique": "High-content epifluorescence imaging / automated microscopy",
      "why": "This high-content imaging system can capture automated tile scans or multi-well images of culture plates to quantify cell confluence, surface coverage, and cell counts via fluorescence or phase imaging over time.",
      "accessories_to_confirm": [
        "appropriate fluorescence filters or labels (e.g., nuclear stain or live cell stain)",
        "environmental control chamber for live-cell imaging if monitoring continuously"
      ]
    },
    {
      "instrument_id": "EQ07",
      "role": "supplementary",
      "technique": "Inverted confocal microscopy",
      "why": "An inverted confocal microscope allows detailed visualization of cells grown on standard culture plates, offering high-resolution imaging of cell morphology and distribution, though it is less suited for automated high-throughput whole-plate coverage tracking.",
      "accessories_to_confirm": [
        "live-cell incubation chamber (temperature and CO2 control)",
        "suitable objective lenses"
      ]
    },
    {
      "instrument_id": "EQ23",
      "role": "supplementary",
      "technique": "Inverted optical microscopy",
      "why": "An inverted optical microscope is useful for routine, qualitative visual checks of cell morphology and overall confluency in culture plates, but lacks automated high-content quantification capabilities.",
      "accessories_to_confirm": [
        "phase contrast objectives",
        "camera attachment for image capture"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "not_available": [],
  "clarifying_question": null,
  "summary": "To track fibroblast cell number and surface coverage over a week in culture plates, the Keyence high-content imaging system (EQ09) can be used as a primary instrument for automated quantification. Inverted microscopes (EQ07 and EQ23) are available as supplementary tools for detailed visual and confluency checks."
}

