  "summary": "To determine the glass transition temperature (Tg) of your amorphous solid dispersion for storage stability, differential scanning calorimetry is the standard primary technique available via EQ18. You can also utilize thermogravimetric analysis (EQ17) to check for sample degradation or residual solvent loss during heating, and a hybrid rheometer (EQ19) for complementary viscoelastic transition measurements."
}

